/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  apalutamide01_tablets -- a drug-product plant: apalutamide 60 mg film-coated
  tablets.  The API is BOUGHT; everything else is made here (DEV.md 4c C97,
  phase A).  A BASE CASE: it runs, it is NOT optimised, and every number a
  group would change is a plain key, said to be an assumption where it is
  declared.  The README is the narrative; this file is the topology.

  THE BASIS (README section 2): 12 800 tablets per hour PRESSED, the flowsheet
  basis, of a 580 mg core carrying 60 mg of apalutamide in 240 mg of a 1:3
  apalutamide:HPMCAS spray-dried dispersion, with a 3 % film coat.  THIS
  STEADY FLOWSHEET IS THE MATERIAL BALANCE PER UNIT OF PRODUCT (DEV.md 4c
  C99): the plant runs in BATCHES (lots of final blend, released one by one)
  and its spray dryer in CAMPAIGNS, and the BATCH PLAN in system/postDict
  sizes each step for one lot from these streams' masses, counts the lots a
  year from the declared production, and finds the step that paces each
  train.  The absolute rate below is a basis -- except for the spray dryer,
  whose hardware this flowsheet models, so its rate IS the dryer's capacity.

    SOLUTION AND SPRAY DRYING (the closed nitrogen loop)
      acetoneFeed -> [acetoneTank] -> acetoneToPrep --+
      apiFeed (BOUGHT) -------------------------------+-> [solutionPrep] -> sprayFeed --+
      hpmcasFeed -------------------------------------+                                  |
                                                                                         v
      n2Makeup --+                                                              [SD] sprayDryer
                 +-> [n2Mix] -> [blower] -> [gasHeater] -> dryingGas ---------->  |       |
      gasRecycle-+     ^                     393 K                               asdPowder  exhaustGas
                       |                                                          |       |
                       |                                              [exhaustCooler] 308 K (cooling water)
                       |                                                          |       |
                       |                                       [solventCondenser] 263 K (NH3 refrigeration)
                       |                                                    |              |
                       |                                          recoveredSolvent      condenserGas
                       |                                                    |              |
                       |                                          [recoveredTank]     [purgeSplit] -> purgeGas (vent)
                       |                                            recoveredAcetone       |
                       +--------------------------------------------------------- gasRecycle (TEAR)

    DRY GRANULATION, TABLETING, COATING, PACKAGING
      asdPowder + MCC + silicified MCC + croscarmellose + silica + MgSt
        -> [blender] -> intraBlend -> [rollerCompactor] -> ribbons -> [mill] -> milledGranules
                                           ^                                          |
                                           +---------- finesRecycle (TEAR) <--- [screen] -> granules
      granules + croscarmellose + MgSt -> [finalBlender] -> finalBlend -> [tabletPress] -> tabletCores
                                                                                    +-> tabletRejects
      water + PVA + PEG + talc + TiO2 + iron oxide -> [coatingSuspensionPrep] -> coatingSuspension
      tabletCores + coatingSuspension -> [coatingPan] -> wetCoatedTablets
      coatingAirIn -> [airHeater] 333 K -> coatingAir
      wetCoatedTablets + coatingAir -> [coatingDryer] -> coatedTablets + coatingExhaust
      coatedTablets -> [packagingLine] -> packagedTablets

  TWO RECYCLES, both declared in system/solverDict: the drying gas
  (gasRecycle) and the compactor fines (finesRecycle).  The recovered
  acetone is NOT recycled in this base case: it goes to a tank, for QC and
  reuse -- the README says why, and closing that loop is a group's question.

  WHAT IS A PLACEHOLDER.  The blenders, the roller compactor, the mill, the
  screen, the tablet press and the packaging line are FLOW PRIMITIVES (a
  `mixer`, a `splitter`): they conserve mass and energy and model NOTHING of
  the machine -- no blend uniformity, no ribbon density, no particle-size
  reduction, no compaction force, no tablet hardness.  Choupo has no such
  equipment model; none is invented here.  The coating pan is TWO boxes, a
  `mixer` (the spray lands on the cores) and a `solidDryer` (the hot air
  takes the water off), which is the mass and energy balance of one machine.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

units
(
    //  ===================== SOLUTION AND SPRAY DRYING =====================

    //  ---- the fresh-acetone tank ------------------------------------------
    //  The solvent is bought in bulk and held before use: 14 days is an
    //  AUTHOR-SET ASSUMPTION (a delivery cycle plus a safety stock), declared
    //  HERE and nowhere else -- the tank in system/postDict links this unit.
    {
        name        acetoneTank;
        type        storageTank;
        in          acetoneFeed;
        outputs     ( acetoneToPrep );
        operation   { residenceTime 14 day;  fillFraction 0.85; }
    }

    //  ---- the solution tank -------------------------------------------------
    //  The bought API and HPMCAS are charged into the acetone in a jacketed
    //  tank held at 25 C (DECLARED: `operation { T ...; }`, so its duty is
    //  published -- nil here, every inlet arrives at 25 C, because the heat
    //  of solution is not modelled).  A `mixer` CARRIES the two powders as
    //  solids (it never dissolves anything -- the README says what that
    //  neglects), and the spray dryer reads dissolved and suspended solids
    //  alike.  The solids content of the spray solution (10 wt %) is set by
    //  the inlet flows in 0/: an AUTHOR-SET ASSUMPTION.
    {
        name        solutionPrep;
        type        mixer;
        inputs      ( apiFeed  hpmcasFeed  acetoneToPrep );
        outputs     ( sprayFeed );
        operation   { T 298.15 K; }
    }

    //  ---- the drying-gas loop: make-up, blower, heater --------------------
    {
        name        n2Mix;
        type        mixer;
        inputs      ( n2Makeup  gasRecycle );
        outputs     ( loopGas );
    }
    {
        //  The loop fan.  Its HARDWARE is its shaft power and efficiency (the
        //  compressor's credo); the pressure it reaches is a RESULT.  That
        //  pressure stands for the drop through the dryer, the cyclone and
        //  filter, and the condenser, none of which is computed.  1 kW and
        //  0.70 are AUTHOR-SET.
        name        blower;
        type        compressor;
        in          loopGas;
        outputs     ( blowerOut );
        operation   { W_shaft 1000;  eta 0.70; }      // W, -
    }
    {
        //  393.15 K (120 C) drying-gas inlet: an AUTHOR-SET ASSUMPTION, of the
        //  order used to dry an organic-solvent solution with an outlet well
        //  above the solvent's dew point.
        name        gasHeater;
        type        phaseChanger;
        in          blowerOut;
        outputs     ( dryingGas );
        operation   { outletT 393.15 K;  P 1.10 bar; }
    }

    //  ---- the spray dryer --------------------------------------------------
    //  Every number in `operation` is HARDWARE, and AUTHOR-SET: a rotary
    //  atomiser and a chamber of the size of a pilot or small production
    //  dryer, nobody's catalogue.  The powder leaves BONE-DRY (no sorption
    //  isotherm of acetone on HPMCAS is declared -- none was found -- so the
    //  residual-moisture model is off, said on the run): the SECONDARY drying
    //  every real ASD needs to bring its residual solvent below its limit is
    //  NOT modelled.  `liquidViscosity` is DECLARED because no record carries
    //  the viscosity of a 10 wt % HPMCAS solution in acetone: 0.02 Pa s is an
    //  AUTHOR-SET guess, twenty times the solvent's (to be measured).
    {
        name        SD;
        type        sprayDryer;
        inputs      ( sprayFeed  dryingGas );
        outputs     ( asdPowder  exhaustGas );
        operation
        {
            wheelDiameter    0.05 m;     // rotary atomiser -- ASSUMED
            wheelSpeed       25000;      // rpm -- ASSUMED
            chamberDiameter  1.2 m;      // drying chamber -- ASSUMED
            chamberHeight    2.5 m;      // -> residence time is a RESULT
            liquidViscosity  0.02;       // Pa s -- ASSUMED, see above
        }
    }

    //  ---- solvent recovery --------------------------------------------------
    {
        //  Cooling water takes the exhaust from its outlet temperature to
        //  308.15 K before the refrigerated condenser, so the refrigeration
        //  only removes what cooling water cannot.  308.15 K: ASSUMED, a
        //  10 K approach to the cooling-water supply.
        name        exhaustCooler;
        type        phaseChanger;
        in          exhaustGas;
        outputs     ( cooledExhaust );
        operation   { outletT 308.15 K;  P 1.10 bar; }
    }
    {
        //  The solvent condenser: the exhaust is chilled to 263.15 K (-10 C)
        //  and the acetone condenses down to its vapour pressure there.  The
        //  temperature is the recovery knob (README section 5): an AUTHOR-SET
        //  ASSUMPTION, against ammonia refrigeration (239.8 K).  The condenser
        //  is the exchanger (its duty is sized and priced); the separator
        //  below is the drum that parts the condensate from the gas.
        name        solventCondenser;
        type        phaseChanger;
        in          cooledExhaust;
        outputs     ( chilledExhaust );
        operation   { outletT 263.15 K;  P 1.0 bar; }
    }
    {
        //  The condensate pot: a flash at the condenser's own outlet state,
        //  so its duty is nil -- it SEPARATES, the condenser cooled.
        name        condensatePot;
        type        isothermalFlash;
        in          chilledExhaust;
        outputs     ( recoveredSolvent  condenserGas );
        operation   { T 263.15 K;  P 1.0 bar; }
    }
    {
        //  A small purge keeps the loop from accumulating what leaks in, and
        //  the nitrogen make-up (0/n2Makeup) replaces it: at steady state the
        //  loop holds make-up / purge fraction of nitrogen.  5 %: ASSUMED.
        //  The purge carries acetone at the condenser's vapour pressure to a
        //  vent treatment the plant does not model (README).
        name        purgeSplit;
        type        splitter;
        in          condenserGas;
        outputs     ( purgeGas  gasRecycle );
        operation   { fractions ( 0.05  0.95 ); }
    }
    {
        //  The recovered acetone is held for testing before reuse: 7 days,
        //  AUTHOR-SET.  It leaves the plant as a declared OUTLET (reused or
        //  sold back), not recycled to the solution tank -- README section 3.
        name        recoveredTank;
        type        storageTank;
        in          recoveredSolvent;
        outputs     ( recoveredAcetone );
        operation   { residenceTime 7 day;  fillFraction 0.85; }
    }

    //  ===================== DRY GRANULATION ================================
    //  Every unit below until the coating is a MASS-BALANCE PLACEHOLDER.
    {
        //  The intragranular blend.  The spray-dried dispersion leaves the
        //  dryer warm and is HELD -- secondary drying and quality-control
        //  release, neither modelled -- so it reaches the blender at room
        //  temperature: the blend is DECLARED at 298.15 K, and the duty that
        //  implies (the heat the warm powder gave the room) is published as
        //  `Q_kW`.  No utility serves it; the run lists it as unserved.
        name        blender;
        type        mixer;
        inputs      ( asdPowder  mccFeed  smccFeed  ccsIntraFeed  silicaFeed  mgstIntraFeed );
        outputs     ( intraBlend );
        operation   { T 298.15 K; }
    }
    {
        name        rollerCompactor;            // PLACEHOLDER: blend + fines -> ribbons
        type        mixer;
        inputs      ( intraBlend  finesRecycle );
        outputs     ( ribbons );
    }
    {
        name        mill;                       // PLACEHOLDER: ribbons -> granules, no size model
        type        splitter;
        in          ribbons;
        outputs     ( milledGranules );
        operation   { fractions ( 1.0 ); }
    }
    {
        //  PLACEHOLDER for the screen: 15 % of the milled material is FINES
        //  returned to the compactor -- AUTHOR-SET.  A `splitter` divides a
        //  flow without changing its composition, which is what a screen does
        //  to a blend in this model (the composition of the fines is the
        //  blend's).
        name        screen;
        type        splitter;
        in          milledGranules;
        outputs     ( granules  finesRecycle );
        operation   { fractions ( 0.85  0.15 ); }
    }

    //  ===================== FINAL BLEND AND TABLETING ======================
    {
        name        finalBlender;               // extragranular disintegrant + lubricant
        type        mixer;
        inputs      ( granules  ccsExtraFeed  mgstExtraFeed );
        outputs     ( finalBlend );
    }
    {
        //  PLACEHOLDER for the press: 1 % of the tablets are REJECTED (weight,
        //  hardness, start-up) -- AUTHOR-SET.  The rejects leave the plant
        //  (README: whether they can be reworked is a GMP question).
        name        tabletPress;
        type        splitter;
        in          finalBlend;
        outputs     ( tabletCores  tabletRejects );
        operation   { fractions ( 0.99  0.01 ); }
    }

    //  ===================== FILM COATING ===================================
    {
        //  The coating suspension: 20 wt % solids in water -- AUTHOR-SET.
        //  The PVA and PEG are carried as solids (nothing dissolves here).
        name        coatingSuspensionPrep;
        type        mixer;
        inputs      ( coatWater  pvaFeed  pegFeed  talcFeed  tio2Feed  feOxFeed );
        outputs     ( coatingSuspension );
        operation   { T 298.15 K; }       // a stirred tank at 25 C, as the solution tank
    }
    {
        //  60 C coating air: AUTHOR-SET, of the order used for aqueous film
        //  coating.  Heated by LP steam.
        name        airHeater;
        type        phaseChanger;
        in          coatingAirIn;
        outputs     ( coatingAir );
        operation   { outletT 333.15 K;  P 1.01325 bar; }
    }
    {
        //  The coating pan, part 1: the suspension lands on the cores.
        name        coatingPan;
        type        mixer;
        inputs      ( tabletCores  coatingSuspension );
        outputs     ( wetCoatedTablets );
    }
    {
        //  The coating pan, part 2: the hot air takes the water off.  A
        //  `solidDryer`: the moisture the tablets keep is set by a sorption
        //  isotherm, declared on the microcrystalline cellulose (the
        //  hygroscopic bulk of the core) in constant/components -- AUTHOR-SET
        //  parameters; every other solid rides through dry, said on the run.
        name        coatingDryer;
        type        solidDryer;
        inputs      ( wetCoatedTablets  coatingAir );
        outputs     ( coatedTablets  coatingExhaust );
    }

    //  ===================== PACKAGING ======================================
    {
        name        packagingLine;              // PLACEHOLDER: bottles / blisters not modelled
        type        splitter;
        in          coatedTablets;
        outputs     ( packagedTablets );
        operation   { fractions ( 1.0 ); }
    }
);

